<% content_for :title, "Shipping | #{current_store.name}" %>
<%= render layout: "pages/legal", locals: { eyebrow: "Legal", title: "Shipping policy" } do %>
  <h2>Where we ship</h2>
  <p>We currently ship to
     <b><%= current_store.shipping_countries.map { |c| country_name(c) rescue c }.to_sentence %></b>.
     If your country is not on the list, the checkout will not let you complete an order — write to us
     and we will tell you whether we can arrange it.</p>

  <h2>What it costs</h2>
  <% if current_store.shipping_cents.zero? %>
    <p>Shipping is <b>free on every order</b>, with no minimum.</p>
  <% else %>
    <p>Shipping is <b><%= MoneyFormatter.format(current_store.shipping_cents, current_store.currency) %></b>
       per parcel.
       <% if current_store.free_shipping_threshold? %>
         Orders over
         <b><%= MoneyFormatter.format(current_store.free_shipping_threshold_cents, current_store.currency) %></b>
         ship free.
       <% end %>
       The fee is charged once per parcel, not per item, so adding a second jar never doubles it.</p>
  <% end %>

  <h2>When it leaves</h2>
  <% window = DispatchWindow.for(current_store) %>
  <p>Orders placed on a working day before <b><%= window.cutoff_at.strftime("%-l %p").strip %></b> are
     prepared the same day. Orders placed after that, or at a weekend, go out on the next working day.
     Dispatch always follows payment confirmation — an order that has not been paid is not prepared.</p>

  <h2>How long it takes</h2>
  <p><mark class="legal__todo">State your real delivery windows per destination, for example "Canada:
     5–9 business days".</mark> These are estimates from the carrier, not guarantees. Customs, weather
     and public holidays can add days, and we cannot shorten them once a parcel has left.</p>

  <h2>Tracking</h2>
  <p>You get a tracking link by email as soon as the carrier scans your parcel. If tracking has not
     moved for five business days, write to <%= mail_to current_store.support_email %> and we will open
     an enquiry with the carrier.</p>

  <h2>Wrong address</h2>
  <p>We ship to the address you enter at checkout. Check it before paying: once a parcel is with the
     carrier we cannot change it. A parcel returned to us because the address was wrong can be
     reshipped, with postage payable again.</p>

  <h2>Lost parcels</h2>
  <p>If tracking shows a parcel as delivered but you have not received it, tell us within 7 days. We
     open an enquiry with the carrier and, once they confirm the loss, we replace or refund the order.</p>

  <h2>Duties and taxes</h2>
  <p><mark class="legal__todo">If you ship outside your own customs union, say clearly whether the
     customer pays import duty on delivery.</mark></p>
<% end %>
